      "text_raw": "In a series of equal struc-\ntures, the first and last ones\nnever quite match. The\nreason is that the first and\nlast ones see different neigh-\nbors. The effects of process-\ning steps such as under-\netching, contact holes, etc.\nwill be different. This is\nwhy dummy transistors (or\ncapacitors) have to be added\nat the beginning and at the\nend. They are not used.\nThey are dummies.\nThis is illustrated next.",
